Done. Here's what I implemented:

### Summary

Problem: edit_file showed a colored diff preview, but write_file just showed "▶ write src/foo.rs (42 lines)" with no visibility into what changed.

Solution: Two changes across two files:

1. **src/format/diff.rs** — Added truncate_diff_preview(diff, max_lines) function that truncates a pre-formatted diff to a configurable number of lines with a "... (N more lines)" summary. Includes 4 tests (empty, short passthrough, exact limit, long truncation).

2. `src/prompt.rs` — In handle_tool_execution_start, added a write_file branch after the existing edit_file block. When the file already exists, reads the old content before the tool writes, computes a diff with format_edit_diff, truncates to 30 lines with truncate_diff_preview, and displays it. Gracefully skips new files, unreadable files, and identical content.

Key design decisions:
• Reads file at ToolExecutionStart (before tool execution) to capture the BEFORE state
• Only fires when file exists (new file creation just shows line count, no diff)
• Silent failure — if read_to_string fails (binary, permissions), no diff shown
• 30-line truncation limit (higher than edit_file's 20 since write_file diffs tend to be larger)
• All CI checks pass: cargo fmt, `cargo clippy -D warnings, cargo build, cargo test` (2532 + 88 tests)

